SUMMARY:Middle Creek Winter Bird Walk
DESCRIPTION:This field trip offers a hands-on birding experience that will 
 allow participants to explore Middle Creek’s winter landscape and observ
 e the season’s local bird species while gaining insight into the process
  of counting birds for the Christmas Bird Count (CBC). Whether you’re a 
 seasoned birder or new to birding and CBCs\, this outing offers a unique o
 pportunity to connect with nature and learn how birding data is collected 
 in the field each year for this citizen-science survey. Pre-registration i
 s required by 5 p.m the day prior for this offering. Contact Ted at tanich
 olsii@gmail.com or 717-856-3851 if you have questions or want to make a re
 servation to attend. IMPORTANT NOTE: Attendees must wear blaze orange for 
 this field trip per new Pennsylvania Game Commission regulations requiring
  wear on Game Lands Oct. 1 through Jan. 31. Location: Middle Creek Wildlif
 e Management Area Visitor Center\, 100 Museum Road\, Stevens\, PA 17578 Co
 ntact: Ted Nichols\, 717-856-3851 or tanicholsii@gmail.com.\n\nPrice: Not 
 supplied by this calendar\; check event details\n\nSchedule listed: Dec 26
